 ## Overview
-Illustrative Volume Rendering with Style Transfer combines standard direct volume ray casting with a Style Transfer Function (STF) to apply artistic, non-photorealistic styles to volumetric data [S1, unofficial]. It allows users to load volumetric datasets, define transfer functions that map density to material indices and styles, and interactively rotate and zoom the rendered result [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from photorealistic ray casting by decoupling the visual appearance (color/texture) from the physical density, using a 2D array texture to map surface normals and material types to pre-computed artistic styles [S1, unofficial].
+Illustrative Volume Rendering with Style Transfer combines standard direct volume ray casting with a Style Transfer Function (STF) to apply artistic styles to volumetric data [S1, unofficial]. It allows users to load volumetric data, save and load transfer functions with assigned styles, and interactively rotate or zoom around the volume [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard ray casting which maps scalar values directly to photorealistic colors, this method maps scalar values to style descriptors that drive the final appearance, enabling non-photorealistic rendering [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method uses a two-pass rendering approach: first, it renders the back face of the volume to determine ray exit points; second, it performs ray casting through the volume, using the exit points to limit ray length and applying style transfer textures to determine the final color [S1, unofficial].
+The method operates on scalar volume values $V(\mathbf{p})$ retrieved at sample positions $\mathbf{p}$ along the ray, building on the shared principles of [Style Transfer and Illustrative Rendering](13031-style-transfer-and-illustrative-rendering.md) and [Transfer Function and Opacity Mapping](2789-transfer-function-and-opacity-mapping.md). It employs a two-pass rendering approach: first rendering the back face to capture exit points, then performing ray casting that utilizes these exit points for ray length calculation, combined with style transfer textures [S1, unofficial].
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Input**: A 3D volume dataset (scalar field), a camera view (projection, view, model matrices), and style transfer textures.
-*   **Output**: A 2D image with artistic styling applied to the volumetric data.
+**Inputs:**
+*   Scalar volume data $V$ (normalized floats).
+*   Style Transfer Function (STF) parameters and styles.
+*   Camera parameters (projection, view, model matrices).
+*   Ray casting parameters: `stepSize` (default 0.001f) and `threshold` (default 0.15f) [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Outputs:**
+*   Final rendered image with artistic style applied.
 
